1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,711
Allen, what did
you just tear up?

2
00:00:02,919 --> 00:00:05,296
Oh, Grandpa,
it's just a painting.

3
00:00:05,296 --> 00:00:06,297
These guys were
trying to give it

4
00:00:06,297 --> 00:00:07,132
to you as a gift.

5
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:09,092
But I couldn't tell
you it was so fake,

6
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,176
I just tore it up.

7
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,554
A fake painting?

8
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:13,638
They said
the painting

9
00:00:13,638 --> 00:00:15,515
was a Picasso, worth
three million dollars.

10
00:00:15,932 --> 00:00:17,017
But I mean,
look at them.

11
00:00:17,934 --> 00:00:19,436
They could not afford
something like that.

12
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:20,437
It has to be a fake.

13
00:00:24,524 --> 00:00:25,567
Picasso...

14
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:28,278
Oh my God.

15
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:29,529
See?

16
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:30,447
Grandpa doesn't
even want

17
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:31,239
that kind of trash

18
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:32,323
messing
up the floor.

19
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,284
You guys better
get out of here.

20
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:35,410
You're not welcome.

21
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:41,499
Allen?

22
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:43,251
Come here.

23
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:43,960
Yes, Grandpa.

24
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:44,544
Closer.

25
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:45,295
Yeah.

26
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:47,130
That's my boy,
that's my boy.

27
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,715
All that
college education.

28
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:50,425
And you turned
out to be

29
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,218
such a big idiot!

30
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,263
Just shut
your mouth!

31
00:00:55,263 --> 00:00:57,140
Why did
you hit me?

32
00:00:57,474 --> 00:01:02,103
You just destroyed
three million dollars,

33
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:02,979
you idiot!

34
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:05,106
Three million dollars?

35
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:06,524
You can't believe
their stories.

36
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,901
-I have been
-Obviously a knockoff.

37
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:08,943
collecting and
it takes longer

38
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:09,736
than you've been alive

39
00:01:09,736 --> 00:01:12,197
and I know
real from fake.

40
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:14,908
It was worth more
than three million

41
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,577
until you ruined it!

42
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:20,371
What? It's real?
